#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# coordinate_bounding_box

#% text
# `coordinate_bounding_box(pts)` gives the corners `[[min x, min y, ...], [max x, max y, ...]]` of the points in `pts`; `coordinate_bounding_box(pts, d)` pads them as `coordinate_bounds` does.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the transpose of `coordinate_bounds`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
coordinate_bounding_box([[0, 1], [1, 2], [2, 1], [3, 2], [4, 0]])
#% output
#= [[0, 0], [4, 2]]

#% cell
coordinate_bounding_box([[3, -3], [3, 3], [-3, 3], [-3, -3]], [1, 2])
#% output
#= [[-4, -5], [4, 5]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `coordinate_bounds`, `coordinate_bounding_box_array`
